{"id": "section-body-23265", "title": "Contrast Induced Nephropathy (CIN)", "chapterId": "chapter-twenty-one", "blocks": [{"id": "body-23265", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Contrast Induced Nephropathy (CIN)", "runs": [{"text": "Contrast"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Induced"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Nephropathy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(CIN)"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "552"}}, {"id": "body-23266", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Contrast induced nephropathy (CIN), which is also known as Contrast Induced Acute Kidney Injury may occur after administration of iodinated contrast material, which is called contrast-induced nephropathy. Common contrast based studies resulting in CIN include CT scan, MRI and coronary angiography. Contrast induced acute kidney injury is usually characterized by rapid recovery of renal function.", "runs": [{"text": "Contrast induced nephropathy (CIN), which is also known as Contrast Induced Acute Kidney Injury may occur after administration of iodinated contrast material, which is called contrast-induced nephropathy. Common contrast based studies resulting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CIN"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "include"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "scan,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "MRI"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "coronary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "angiography."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Contrast"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "induced"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acute"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "kidney"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "injury"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characterized by rapid recovery of renal function."}]}, {"id": "body-23268", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-23269", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Early mild increase in serum creatinine that is generally observed within 24-48 hours after the iodinated contrast exposure and that is usually mild. Serum creatinine starts to decline within 3-7days of exposure", "runs": [{"text": "Early"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mild"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increase"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "serum"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "creatinine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "generally"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "observed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "within"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "24-48"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hours"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "iodinated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "contrast exposure and that is usually mild. Serum creatinine starts to decline within 3-7days of exposure"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "544"}}, {"id": "body-23270", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "No oliguria, patients with CIN are passing urine normally and if it occurs develop immediately. Oliguria and more severe elevation of creatinine may develop in patients with moderate to severe CKD.", "runs": [{"text": "No"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oliguria,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "CIN"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "passing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "urine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "normally"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "if"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occurs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "develop"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immediately."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Oliguria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "more"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe elevation of creatinine may develop in patients with moderate to severe CKD."}], "